oroborus for Debian
-------------------

UPDATE: Oroborus no longer has a current maintainer upstream. There is a beta
version available that is decently stable and has more features. I am_not
going to create any official packages of this new version. However there
is an unofficial package at http://people.debian.org/~brandon/

The author of Oroborus was kind enuf to create somewhat of a users guide. This
came in the origonal source and was packaged with oroborus. You can find it in
/usr/share/doc/oroborus/doc.

Oroborus does not have a menu of any kind. This is why I suggest you install
the package 'deskmenu'. It allows for a root menu at the click of a mouse and
is fairly configureable. Sometimes a menu is useful ;)

Oroborus does not configure a mouse cursor other than the default 'X'. For
those of you who do not know how to change your mouse cursor add these lines in
your .xinitrc file before the line that starts oroborus

# this sets the root cursor image
bitmaps="/usr/include/X11/bitmaps"
xsetroot -cursor $bitmaps/left_ptr $bitmaps/left_ptrmsk &

Alternatively if you are planning on using gnome-session to run Oroborus then
let Gnome handle the cursor bitmap for you :)

The theme converter script written by the same auther as oroborus is located in
/usr/share/doc/oroborus/examples. This should be used to convert old-style
themes to the newer style.

Did I forget anything?

 -- Brandon L. Griffith <brandon@debian.org>, Tue,  7 Aug 2001 23:20:57 -0400
